{"answer": "Yes, master mode is supported. The I2C module includes a \"MASTER PROCESS\" state, allowing the device to control the bus as either a master-receiver or master-transmitter [S5]. Additionally, the module supports multi-master mode and high-speed mode, with specific registers like `FDIVCFG` and `FDIVHIGHCFG` used for baudrate generation in master mode [S1].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "Is the master mode supported?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 5, "bm25_score": 5.8886115795999565, "chunk_index": 8, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1383, "page_start": 1383, "score": -0.03076923076923077, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 5}, {"bm25_rank": 8, "bm25_score": 4.255612973879256, "chunk_index": 24, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1396, "page_start": 1396, "score": -0.030330882352941176, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 7, "bm25_score": 4.320545131887222, "chunk_index": 23, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1395, "page_start": 1395, "score": -0.029211087420042643, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 10}, {"bm25_rank": 9, "bm25_score": 4.2479421906777945, "chunk_index": 22, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1395, "page_start": 1395, "score": -0.028985507246376812, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 9}, {"bm25_rank": 10, "bm25_score": 4.218026932401931, "chunk_index": 15, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1390, "page_start": 1390, "score": -0.028370221327967807, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 11}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T13:22:27.972561+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The supported data transfer rates for the I2C module are:\n\n*   **Standard mode:** Up to 100 kbit/s (range: 20 kbit/s to 100 kbit/s) [S1][S4].\n*   **Fast mode:** Up to 400 kbit/s (range: 100 kbit/s to 400 kbit/s) [S1][S4].\n*   **High-speed mode:** Up to 3.4 Mbit/s (range: 500 kbit/s to 3.4 Mbit/s) [S1][S4].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "What are the supported data transfer rates?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 8.37523532313412, "chunk_index": 2, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1377, "page_start": 1377, "score": -0.031024531024531024, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 6}, {"bm25_rank": 9, "bm25_score": 6.0041772244212765, "chunk_index": 3, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1378, "page_start": 1378, "score": -0.03036576949620428, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 28, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1399, "page_start": 1399, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 9.266321869885756, "chunk_index": 0, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1375, "page_start": 1375, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 44, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1414, "page_start": 1414, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T13:22:30.449171+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The start and stop conditions are realized through specific signal transitions on the SDA and SCL lines, occurring while the SCL line remains at a high level [S1].\n\n*   **Start Condition:** This is indicated by a high-to-low transition on the SDA line while the SCL line is high. This condition marks the beginning of communication and sets the bus state to busy [S1].\n*   **Stop Condition:** This is defined by a low-to-high transition on the SDA line while the SCL line is high. This condition closes the transmission and sets the bus state to free again [S1].\n\nThese conditions are generated by the master device [S1]. In high-speed mode, while stop and restart conditions are still used, no start condition appears; instead, a master code is used to initiate communication [S5].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "How are the start and stop conditions realized?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 9.931983935618373, "chunk_index": 2, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1377, "page_start": 1377, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 7.191219236504432, "chunk_index": 3, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1378, "page_start": 1378, "score": -0.031754032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 7.571655416916075, "chunk_index": 9, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1384, "page_start": 1384, "score": -0.031746031746031744, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 6, "bm25_score": 7.015950839256919, "chunk_index": 5, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1380, "page_start": 1380, "score": -0.02964426877470356, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 9}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 9.64761511703, "chunk_index": 7, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1382, "page_start": 1382, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T13:22:33.339744+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "To perform 10-bit slave addressing in I2C, follow these steps:\n\n**1. Configuration**\n*   Set the `TBAM` (Two Byte Address Mode) bit in the Address Configuration Register (`ADDRCFG`) to select 10-bit addressing [S2].\n*   Write the 10-bit device address to bits [9:0] of the `ADR` field in the `ADDRCFG` register [S2].\n\n**2. Address Transmission Protocol**\nThe 10-bit addressing scheme uses a reserved preamble address \"11110XX\", where \"XX\" represents the two most significant bits of the 10-bit address [S1][S3].\n\n*   **Writing to Slave:**\n    1.  Transmit a Start condition.\n    2.  Transmit the first address byte: Preamble \"11110XX\" with the RnW bit set to 0 [S1].\n    3.  Wait for an acknowledge from the matching slave [S1].\n    4.  Transmit the second address byte: The eight least significant bits of the 10-bit address [S1].\n    5.  Wait for an acknowledge. Only the slave matching the combined 10-bit address will acknowledge [S1].\n    6.  Transmit data bytes until a Stop or Restart condition [S1].\n\n*   **Reading from Slave:**\n    A combined format with a Restart condition is required [S1]:\n    1.  **Write Phase:** Transmit the 10-bit address as described above (Preamble with RnW=0, followed by the second address byte) [S1].\n    2.  **Restart Phase:** Generate a Repeated Start condition (Sr) [S1].\n    3.  **Read Phase:** Transmit the preamble address \"11110XX\" again, but this time with the RnW bit set to 1 [S1]. The matching slave remembers it was addressed previously and will acknowledge, allowing the master to receive data [S1].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "How to do the 10-bit slave addressing?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 11.488768448902922, "chunk_index": 6, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1381, "page_start": 1381, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 8.611004625945794, "chunk_index": 65, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1435, "page_start": 1435, "score": -0.03200204813108039, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 10.012882921391707, "chunk_index": 3, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1378, "page_start": 1378, "score": -0.031754032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 6, "bm25_score": 7.950334838305357, "chunk_index": 73, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1443, "page_start": 1443, "score": -0.029236022193768675, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 11}, {"bm25_rank": 12, "bm25_score": 6.355555283764539, "chunk_index": 74, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1444, "page_start": 1444, "score": -0.028594771241830064, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 8}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T13:22:47.248077+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "Based on the provided context, the operational mode of the I2C module (Configuration Mode or Run Mode) is selected using the **RUN** bit.\n\n*   **Configuration Mode:** The peripheral is in this mode when bit **RUN** is set to 0.\n*   **Run Mode:** The peripheral is in this mode when bit **RUN** is set to 1.\n\n[S1]", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "Which register is used to select the operational mode?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 7, "bm25_score": 8.187677058455513, "chunk_index": 59, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1429, "page_start": 1429, "score": -0.03131881575727918, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 8, "bm25_score": 8.187468843261367, "chunk_index": 23, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1395, "page_start": 1395, "score": -0.029411764705882353, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 8}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 11.200583115555576, "chunk_index": 55, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1425, "page_start": 1425, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 47, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1417, "page_start": 1417, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 9.129721094373284, "chunk_index": 10, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1385, "page_start": 1385, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T13:22:48.828737+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "Based on the provided context, the **TPS bit-field** in the **TPSCTRL register** is used to trigger the data transmission.\n\nWriting the packet size to this bit-field indicates that the software wants to transmit a data packet, which initiates the whole data transfer by causing the FIFO unit to assert burst requests [S4]. This action is allowed only if the bus status and RnW bits identify the slave-transmitter mode [S1].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "Which bit is used to trigger the data transmission?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 10.75542544492074, "chunk_index": 17, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1392, "page_start": 1392, "score": -0.03125763125763126, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 5}, {"bm25_rank": 8, "bm25_score": 9.62401289919616, "chunk_index": 44, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1414, "page_start": 1414, "score": -0.03057889822595705, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 10.190597250514784, "chunk_index": 25, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1396, "page_start": 1396, "score": -0.029910714285714284, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 10}, {"bm25_rank": 10, "bm25_score": 9.383652474634003, "chunk_index": 30, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1401, "page_start": 1401, "score": -0.029437229437229435, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 6}, {"bm25_rank": 9, "bm25_score": 9.390920593878292, "chunk_index": 20, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1393, "page_start": 1393, "score": -0.028381642512077296, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 12}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T13:22:53.574884+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "Based on the provided context, there are two Identification Registers mentioned with different addresses depending on the specific register name or context:\n\n1.  The **Module Identification Register** (referred to as `MODID`) is located at address **10004H** [S1].\n2.  The **Module Identification Register** (referred to as `ID` under Global Module Control Registers) is located at address **00008H** [S3].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "What is the address of the Identification Register?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 12.45412726200214, "chunk_index": 54, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1424, "page_start": 1424, "score": -0.03252247488101534, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 12.018776227716911, "chunk_index": 85, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1455, "page_start": 1455, "score": -0.03021353930031804, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 11}, {"bm25_rank": 9, "bm25_score": 9.21953709555895, "chunk_index": 63, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1433, "page_start": 1433, "score": -0.030117753623188408, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 8, "bm25_score": 9.294670102743972, "chunk_index": 18, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1392, "page_start": 1392, "score": -0.028594771241830064, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 12}, {"bm25_rank": 12, "bm25_score": 8.914845166698345, "chunk_index": 65, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1435, "page_start": 1435, "score": -0.028381642512077296, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 9}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T13:22:55.454439+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The provided context does not mention a \"GCE\" bit in the ADDRCFG register. The context mentions the following bits in the ADDRCFG register:\n\n*   **MCE (Master Code Enable):** When set, the device checks if the transmitted address byte is a master code, or configures the device to react to a master code to change the baud rate to high-speed (Hs) mode [S1][S2].\n*   **SOPE (Stop On Packet End):** When set to 1, the transfer is closed by putting a stop condition on the bus [S1][S5].\n\nTherefore, the provided context is not sufficient to answer what the GCE bit represents, as it is not described in the text.", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "What does GCE bit of ADDRCFG register represent?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 7, "bm25_score": 7.204668943644426, "chunk_index": 22, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1395, "page_start": 1395, "score": -0.031054405392392875, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 6, "bm25_score": 7.303460079438393, "chunk_index": 18, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1392, "page_start": 1392, "score": -0.029857397504456328, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 8}, {"bm25_rank": 11, "bm25_score": 5.0762240366683855, "chunk_index": 60, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1430, "page_start": 1430, "score": -0.028577260665441927, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 9}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 73, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1443, "page_start": 1443, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 10.373708930221929, "chunk_index": 25, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1396, "page_start": 1396, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T13:22:58.093547+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The provided context does not explicitly state which interrupts are \"recommended\" to be enabled. It only describes the configuration registers and their reset states:\n\n*   **Protocol Interrupts:** After reset, all protocol interrupt sources (Address Match, General Call, Master Code, Arbitration Lost, Not-acknowledge Received, Transmission End, Receive Mode) are enabled by default in the `PIRQSM` register (Reset Value: `0000 007FH`) [S1].\n*   **Error Interrupts:** After reset, all error interrupt sources (RX FIFO Underflow, RX FIFO Overflow, TX FIFO Underflow, TX FIFO Overflow) are enabled by default in the `ERRIRQSM` register (Reset Value: `0000 000FH`) [S5].\n*   **Interrupt Mask Control:** In the `IMSC` register, all interrupt requests (Last Single Request, Single Request, Last Burst Request, Burst Request, I2C Error, I2C Protocol) are disabled after reset (Reset Value: `0000 0000H`) [S2].", "base_url": "http://106.106.152.161:4000/v1", "candidate_k": 12, "chunks": "data/chunks_i2c_ch34.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "code", "question": "Which interrupts are recommended to be enabled?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 9.543068351497523, "chunk_index": 84, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1454, "page_start": 1454, "score": -0.03252247488101534, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 7, "bm25_score": 6.541409507755434, "chunk_index": 77, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1447, "page_start": 1447, "score": -0.031054405392392875, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 5, "bm25_score": 7.3368192994815935, "chunk_index": 45, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1415, "page_start": 1415, "score": -0.029877369007803793, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 9}, 